From ceb84238e872b18a2d806e4b5c2fa27b8267478a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josh Hoffer <jhoffer@sansorgan.es>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 09:54:48 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] usb: xhci: dbc: advance the transfer ring's dequeue
 pointer

Since commit 7ee645963075 ("usb: xhci: remove legacy 'num_trbs_free'
tracking"), xhci_dbc_queue_bulk_tx() checks for room with
xhci_num_trbs_free(), which measures from the enqueue pointer to
ring->dequeue. Nothing in the DbC driver moves ring->dequeue, though:
the counter that commit removed was the only record of completed TRBs.

So each DbC transfer ring fills after one lap, about 254 TRBs, and every
later queue attempt fails with "failed to queue trbs". ttyDBC goes quiet
after roughly 254 KiB in either direction.

Advance ring->dequeue past each TRB the transfer event handler gives
back, stepping over the link TRB at the end of the segment.

Found on 6.18.64 against an emulation of the debug capability in QEMU;
mainline has the same code.

Fixes: 7ee645963075 ("usb: xhci: remove legacy 'num_trbs_free' tracking")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Josh Hoffer <jhoffer@sansorgan.es>
---
 drivers/usb/host/xhci-dbgcap.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/host/xhci-dbgcap.c b/drivers/usb/host/xhci-dbgcap.c
index e2e0694..f999503 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/host/xhci-dbgcap.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/host/xhci-dbgcap.c
@@ -845,6 +845,15 @@ static void dbc_handle_xfer_event(struct xhci_dbc *dbc, union xhci_trb *event)
 		break;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * The xHC is done with this TRB and any No-op TRBs before it: move the
+	 * dequeue pointer past it, or xhci_num_trbs_free() never sees the
+	 * space come back and the ring fills after one lap.
+	 */
+	ring->dequeue = req->trb + 1;
+	if (TRB_TYPE_LINK_LE32(ring->dequeue->link.control))
+		ring->dequeue = ring->deq_seg->trbs;
+
 	req->actual = req->length - remain_length;
 	xhci_dbc_giveback(req, status);
 }
